Input: {"question": "When was the National Indian Association formed?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 0, "end": 46, "text": "Indian elected representation in legislatures."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 47, "end": 212, "text": "The Reform Association faction on July 26, 1876 established a \"Bharat Sabha\" with Bengali leaders like Surendranath Banerjee, Sivanath Sastri, Ananda Mohan Bose etc."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 213, "end": 262, "text": "and held its first annual conference in Calcutta."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 263, "end": 300, "text": "Initially under Sen it was pro-Crown."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 301, "end": 458, "text": "However, after the 2nd Brahmo Schism of 1878, the Sadharan Brahmo Samaj regrouped with Adi Brahmo Samaj to promote nationalism and freedom from British rule."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 459, "end": 582, "text": "From 1880 till 1890 a bitter battle for control of the Reform Association ensued between the pro-Sen and anti-Sen factions."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d00", "start": 583, "end": 648, "text": "After the death of Sen in 1884 the Reform Association also passed"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d01", "start": 0, "end": 46, "text": "Indian elected representation in legislatures."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0384-79007962fb4f:d01", "start": 47, "end": 212, "text": "The Reform Association faction on July 26, 1876 established a \"Bharat Sabha\" with Bengali leaders like Surendranath Banerjee, Sivanath Sastri, Ananda Mohan Bose etc."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "